snooze (2.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename the 2.5 'insecure' setting to 'ssl_verify' (default true), so the
    config reads as a positive statement instead of a double negative. The old
    name still works, in the file and as SNOOZE_INSECURE, and is translated
    with a warning naming the replacement.

 -- Robert Tulke <rt@ttyS0.sh>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 21:00:00 +0200

snooze (2.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Report a TLS certificate that fails verification as a configuration fault
    naming the likely cause and the ways out, instead of a raw urlopen error,
    and stop retrying a handshake that cannot succeed.
  * Add the 'insecure' setting (SNOOZE_INSECURE) to skip certificate
    verification for a Zabbix whose self-signed certificate can't be added to
    the system trust store. It warns on stderr on every run while set.
  * Skip a config file that exists but can't be read, with a warning, instead
    of letting it mask the files below it. configparser ignores unopenable
    files silently, so an unreadable /etc/snooze.conf looked exactly like a
    missing token and no lower-priority file was ever tried.
  * Name the config file actually in use when no token is set, rather than
    always pointing at /etc/snooze.conf.

 -- Robert Tulke <rt@ttyS0.sh>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0200

snooze (2.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add -n/--dry-run: resolve targets and look up windows as usual, but hold
    back every call that would create, update or delete a maintenance window.
  * Refuse a mute longer than 365 days, reject a url that is neither http nor
    https, and warn when the token would travel over plain http.
  * Report a bad numeric config value (retries, timeout, confirm_threshold)
    as an error instead of a traceback, and keep --json producing a document
    even when an unexpected exception escapes.
  * unmute now removes every maintenance window carrying the target's name,
    so a duplicate created elsewhere can no longer keep a host muted.
  * JSON: every row now has "target" and "type". This renames the "host" and
    "group" keys that "list hosts"/"list groups" used in 2.3.

 -- Robert Tulke <rt@ttyS0.sh>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200

snooze (2.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add --json: one machine-readable document on stdout instead of text,
    with language-independent field names so scripts survive a locale change.
  * Add an example Ansible playbook that mutes a host, upgrades its packages
    and unmutes it again, covering apt, dnf, yum, zypper, pacman and apk.

 -- Robert Tulke <rt@ttyS0.sh>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 09:40:00 +0200

snooze (2.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Read targets from stdin automatically when stdin is not a TTY.
  * Split the documentation into README (landing page) and REFERENCE
    (full command reference), both in English and German.
  * Document the fully qualified Homebrew install path, since the formula
    name collides with homebrew-core's unrelated snooze.

